# Print the matrix
print(m2)
```
Answer:The matrix m2 contains the same numbers as m1, but the arrangement is different. The byrow = TRUE argument tells R to fill the matrix row by row instead of column by column.

scores <- matrix(c(88, 92, 79, 95, 84, 90), nrow = 2, ncol = 3, byrow = TRUE)
rownames(scores) <- c("Quiz1", "Quiz2")
